{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human","id":997469,"title":"Can a Nephandi still be human?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-02T17:58:13-07:00","id":997469,"title":"Can a Nephandi still be human?","content":"i always seen the Nephandi/Barrabi as inhuman as fuck. individuals who love the evil that they do and that are pretty much &quot;Randall Flagg&quot; in the sense that they are evil and they fucking know it. painting rooms with human blood in the shape of pentagrams and such.<br /> <br /> But. is it possible for a Barrabi to know what he is doing but also to be &quot;Human&quot;, to keep a family, kids. to go to work and so on, but knowing that his life is to serve The Darkness and avoid the corruption from touching his loved ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:58:47-07:00","id":997498,"title":"","content":"It isn't impossible, but hard and usually short-lived.<br /> <br /> The idea behind those are of an utterly corrupted state. Or, otherwise presented, you can think of them as diseased. They aren't inhuman in the sense of not being human in body or mind, but they are literally sick people, and their mental issues are going a long way in the sense of corroding any relationship they still have with sane people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T20:03:11-07:00","id":997520,"title":"","content":"Only the extremely naive would pass through the Cauls and expect to live a normal life afterwards. Accepting corruption into you like that and allowing your avatar to be inverted changes you. Even if you get cold feat afterwards and try to resume a normal life, the stench of corruption follows you everywhere. Even the most mundane of sleepers will be able to pick up on it if around you long enough, and will start be uncomfortable around you, unless they too are able to become corrupt.<br /> <br /> That being said, the majority of Barrabi can only turn if they have a specific mindset while entering the Cauls. This can be a simple state of sociopathy and the oh so stereotypical love of destruction. It could be a state of nihilism to the Nth degree, a feeling that everything is meaningless, ascension is a lie dreamed up by the gullible, and oblivion is the only true future the universe has. It could be an active hatred of all things human, a view that humanity is a disease unto itself, only capable of wretched acts of pain, hurt, and depravity; that none are worthy of ascension, and that death is far too good for them. It could also be a real sense of devotion to something infernal, the wyrm, some cosmic horror, or even the concept of oblivion itself. It could even be a sense of devotion to one of the leaders of the Labyrinth, the Gilledian who seem to have all the answers, or at least all the power.<br /> <br /> I don't think any of these mindsets are really compatible with a &quot;normal&quot; life. Any normal life a Nephandus tries to have will most likely be as a way to disguise what they are from suspicious mages, as well as use family connections to increase their spheres of influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:10:49-07:00","id":997554,"title":"","content":"No, an Infernal Mage can still be human (if pathetic or tragic), but Nephandi go one step beyond (they go from selling their soul to transforming it). Kuei-jin are more human than Nephandi, and they have a demon riding their soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:03:58-07:00","id":997567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=997554#post997554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, an Infernal Mage can still be human (if pathetic or tragic), but Nephandi go one step beyond (they go from selling their soul to transforming it). Kuei-jin are more human than Nephandi, and they have a demon riding their soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ding! Infernalists can easily be very human, and most probably are. Many are people who think they can accomplish good if they make little compromises. Those compromises gradually increase, until they are sacrificing bums because, hey, they were heroin-addicts and likely to die in a year or two anyway. At least this way, the Infernalist gets to send his daughter to the best schools, where she will learn to make the world a better place than that bum ever would have.<br /> <br /> Nephandi aren't simple Infernalists. Something has been done to them that leaves them without a remotely human soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T02:12:11-07:00","id":997616,"title":"","content":"It might well be possible, but it's pretty incoherent as a philosophy.<br /> <br /> I mean, the entire point of the Nephandi philosophy is that the Absolute (I think that's the word) touches everything, including the Nephandus themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T02:38:22-07:00","id":997620,"title":"","content":"Could a Nephandus maintain a &quot;normal&quot; life? A relationship? Raise children? Hold down a job? Own a house?<br /> <br /> Certainly, in the same way that a high-functioning psychopath can. Indeed, Nephandi would be a lot easier to spot if they were incapable of acting normal consistently enough. So it's fully possible, though the Nephandus would consider it false and hollow. Their lover would only be kept around for the gratification the Nephandus could gain from them, and to maintain appearances. I would suspect many of them would be slowly turned into mindless thralls, sooner or later.<br /> <br /> Children would be more difficult to justify, unless the Barrabi already had them before the Caul. Nephandi are driven by Anti-Life, so bringing new ones into the world would only make sense if their parent raised them to be pawns in their schemes. Some might be abusive to them, but others might be able to <i>act</i> like loving parents enough to ensure the children's loyalty.<br /> <br /> Owning a house and keeping a job seem like trivial matters - many Nephandi who live undercover likely do it all the time. If a Fallen Mage can remain undetected among non-Fallen Mages, then doing it around sleepers is child's play. The main obstacles are the Nephandus's patience, and their ability to act on their anti-social urges without getting caught.<br /> <br /> And that's really the bottom line. Nephandi are driven towards vile, destructive causes, but are rational enough to maintain the veneer of civility. To them, a &quot;Normal&quot; life is just a tool, with which they pursue their true passion: Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T03:16:37-07:00","id":997621,"title":"","content":"I prefer my Nephandi to be relatable and human, to tempt my players on a meta-level.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I have them as Mages who have been fed up with it all, people who see how the Technocracy and the Traditions both give their <i>everything</i> to make a better world for the Sleepers, and then they take a look at the world of shit and suck and filth and waste, that they are given back.<br /> <br /> The conclusion that a person in a better mental place might say would be: &quot;I must try harder.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Nephandus goes: &quot;The Sleepers don't deserve the world that their betters attempt to create for them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Examples of Nephandi I have explicitly used to my players, include Captain Walker from Spec Ops: The Line, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T03:58:51-07:00","id":997625,"title":"","content":"Human or normal?<br /> Normal they definitely aren't and can't keep that semblance on the long term unless it's for something very specific.<br /> <br /> Human...human they are. One might see the atrocities and think only a monster can do it.<br /> Nope. Human did it. The limits for how high or low they can go is pretty scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T04:39:27-07:00","id":997631,"title":"","content":"But they are spiritually no longer human. They joined with Corruption and, while a normal psychopath is a cancer cell, they are a virus that causes cells to turn cancerous. A Sabbat follower of the Paths is more human than a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Humans are capable of rationalizing practically any evil, but Nephandi do not need to rationalize. Their corrupted souls sing with revelation with every innocent they violate. A Nephandi will not just rape children because they enjoy the crying, they will do so because they understand that every child they violate pushes society ever close to oblivion.<br /> <br /> Nephandi do not necessarily kill, they corrupt and violate. For example, a Nephandi will infiltrate a fraternity and, through conversation, will encourage rape and violence among its members while making them Infernal Sorcerers. Within a year, the Nephandi transforms a group of sixty men with five potential rapists into a group of sixty serial killers who use their crimes as bargaining tools with the Demon Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:02:28-07:00","id":997672,"title":"","content":"Is it not more fearsome if Nephandi are still human?<br /> <br /> It is easy to picture a inhuman fiend as evil.<br /> <br /> And what are Nephandi if not the dark reflections of the ascending Mages.<br /> If they aren't human, then Mages ain't either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Typo 11-03-2016, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:25:52-07:00","id":997678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=997672#post997672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they aren't human, then Mages ain't either.</div> </div> </div> </div>If being human is defined by one's limitations. Then yes, I'd agree that Mages aren't really human anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:47:28-07:00","id":997728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=997678#post997678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If being human is defined by one's limitations. Then yes, I'd agree that Mages aren't really human anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>But until they reach Ascension they act, feel and think like a all too human being. They are torn between two worlds and often their less than ideal needs take the driver's seat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:00:01-07:00","id":997731,"title":"","content":"One senior member of Batini had husband who became Nephandi, but afterwards tried to behave as if it was business as usual - but she saw his corrupted Avatar and killed him. (And tried to redeem the Avatar)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=997631#post997631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nephandi do not necessarily kill, they corrupt and violate. For example, a Nephandi will infiltrate a fraternity and, through conversation, will encourage rape and violence among its members while making them Infernal Sorcerers. Within a year, the Nephandi transforms a group of sixty men with five potential rapists into a group of sixty serial killers who use their crimes as bargaining tools with the Demon Lords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he make all sixty of them into Infernal Sorcerers? If so, that's a mighty Nephandus indeed!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:40:43-07:00","id":997747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=997731#post997731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he make all sixty of them into Infernal Sorcerers? If so, that's a mighty Nephandus indeed!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would figure that only one to three of the Frat guys is actually trained in summoning demons, or in Infernal Sorcery Paths. The rest participate in the big rituals the Frat organizes, and some of its higher ranked ones might have traded parts of their souls for Investments. Most of them are Infernal cultists but not necessarily Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> This is probably the most economical solution, since it keeps the pawns who actually know enough to be a threat to an absolute minimum. Makes the group as a whole more centralized around the core Infernalist Frat guys, and thus easier to control.<br /> <br /> Would require fewer copies of Infernalist tomes to be passed around, as well. While this does mean it's harder for Infernalism as a whole to spread, it also means there are fewer bits of direct evidence that can be traced back to the Nephandus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:55:37-07:00","id":997775,"title":"","content":"And the Nephandi maximizes the spread of corruption. If the Nephandi spends a year teaching three Infernal Sorcerers (and turning the rest into cultists), then you have sixty serial killers organized into three cells (one for each Infernal Sorcerer). Only the leaders of each cell would be associated with the Nephandi, meaning that the Nephandi could 'help' other groups develop their corruption.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi would probably organizing the cultists into a structure that would create maximum corruption. After the introductory years, the cult would start kidnap four teenage girls every moon and, over the course of the moon, each member would ritually violate three of the four teenage girls and make the fourth teenage girl witness every violation. At the end of the moon, they would ritually sacrifice the untouched teenage girl to their Demon Lord patron and make the three violated teenage girls witness the final ceremony. After the ceremony, they would drop the violated girls in a safe place, call up the newspapers on a burner cell phone to tell them where the teenage girls are, and kidnap the next four teenage girls.<br /> <br /> The reason to allow three of the fourth girls to survive is to allow the tales of sacrifice and violation to spread throughout the local community from multiple points of view. After the first month, people would start to worry about their teenage daughters. After the second month, people would start to demand that the authorities start to round up the usual suspects. After the third month, people would start to form vigilante mobs to hunt down the cultists. Within a year after the end of the introductory year, local society has broken down and dozens (if not hundreds) of people have been attacked by vigilantes who are trying to find and stop the cultists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:02:55-07:00","id":998227,"title":"","content":"My image of them has always been as part of the entirely evil group. I think there is an enjoyable aspect in some relatable, human evils. Things that we can understand. But that's never really been my idea of a Nephandi (which might be off). I'd put it akin to a Black Spiral Dancer. Dancing the Spiral (or entering a caul) so utterly changes them as to make their mind somewhat alien. An unrepentant evil that's beyond saving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T08:13:11-07:00","id":998229,"title":"","content":"To echo what Monalfie said, aren't the really low ranking members of any given Nephanic organization the only human ones? The stooges, the mooks, and the deluded sheep are the ones motivated by petty evils. After one's avatar gets inverted the Nephandus is more of a puppet of whatever for of corruption he/she has chosen to serve and eventually embody, and those are usually pretty inhumanly Bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:30:55-07:00","id":998608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=997631#post997631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they are spiritually no longer human. They joined with Corruption and, while a normal psychopath is a cancer cell, they are a virus that causes cells to turn cancerous. A Sabbat follower of the Paths is more human than a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Humans are capable of rationalizing practically any evil, but Nephandi do not need to rationalize. Their corrupted souls sing with revelation with every innocent they violate. A Nephandi will not just rape children because they enjoy the crying, they will do so because they understand that every child they violate pushes society ever close to oblivion.<br /> <br /> Nephandi do not necessarily kill, they corrupt and violate. For example, a Nephandi will infiltrate a fraternity and, through conversation, will encourage rape and violence among its members while making them Infernal Sorcerers. Within a year, the Nephandi transforms a group of sixty men with five potential rapists into a group of sixty serial killers who use their crimes as bargaining tools with the Demon Lords.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get the belief that this was halfway aimed at my &quot;Nephandi are sympathetic post&quot;, so I'll respond like it was that:<br /> <br /> The game that I've been running since 1999 is not a game where objectively evil mages who are evil because they are evil will have any impact, because it's a game with basis heavily in questioning the world and questioning morality. If I use a mage who kicks puppies and murders people for the sake of being an asshole, my players will murder him and go &quot;wow, nice switch to DnD there ManusDomine&quot;, and possibly laugh at me.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Nephandi who act like human beings can get the players to question whether they are in the right, during a given situation or not. For example: I had a war veteran who had grown weary of killing (what he saw as) the same enemy in different clothes over and over, and had simply decided that humanity didn't deserve to exist any more, having seen personally how the effects of warfare looked. He was a broken man, and he had absolutely no chance at reaching his goal of anihilating humanity, even if the players didn't intervene. But he did give us this scene:<br /> <br /> Nephandus (missing a leg and lying on the ground): &quot;Why are you doing this? Can't you see they're a <i>disease</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Suzanne Bachmayer, Damage Control Agent: &quot;Because I must, and because I cannot allow someone like you to destroy everything we have worked for.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nephandus: &quot;But can't you see what they have <i>done?</i> They take beauty and make it into weapons! They take men and make them into hollow puppets of war, who would rather kill and smile than talk to another human! They tear apart the guts of nature and use the waste for weapons! <i>Why do you condone this!?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Suzanne (now aiming her Mjolnir at his forehead): &quot;Because the vision of humanity you have seen, is the vision of a soldier, looking at the waste of humanity, while the vision I have seen, is the vision of an a doctor who knows her duty. I cannot let you live, because to do so would be to lay judgement on an entire species for the actions of a minority and beyond me. I would rather let COMMAND sit with the button that creates the apocalypse than I would that anyone else possesses it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nephandus (now crying): &quot;But can't you see!? The only purpose of humanity is to breed so that they can murder so that they can breed and murder even more! There is no greater purpose than this! Letting them live is a cruelty! A deliberate torture of the world! You are not sparing innocents that cannot defend themselves! You are condoning murderers and rapists and monsters that haven't yet tasted the sweetness of hatred! Why are you <i>DOING THIS!?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Suzanne (fires the pistol and ends him in one shot): &quot;Because if not the Union? Who then?&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously neither of these have a perfect idea of what the world is supposed to look like, and obviously the Union isn't necessarily good, but this situation outlines perfectly what I want from Mage; which is people with good intentions doing horrible things &quot;for a higher cause&quot; and &quot;a better world&quot; no matter the cost. And in this vision of the world, Nephandi are people who have played the zero-sum game and realized the Objective Truth (just like the Traditions' Objective Truths and the Union's Objective Truth...) that mankind isn't worth it, and that burning it down would be the best option.<br /> <br /> But they don't necessarily act like corruptive assholes, who rape and kill and murder. In fact, rather many of them are upstanding moral paragons.<br /> <br /> But this is by no means the canon Nephandi, since my game is heavily houseruled anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 11-05-2016, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T01:26:19-07:00","id":998648,"title":"","content":"I'd say at least a part of canon Nephandi are like that.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a> uses antagonists in much the same way I do: to make an impact on the story, to question the \u201ctruth\u201c, and to deliver an alternative mindset/vantage point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T01:40:27-07:00","id":998652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=998648#post998648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a> uses antagonists in much the same way I do: to make an impact on the story, to question the \u201ctruth\u201c, and to deliver an alternative mindset/vantage point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this.<br /> <br /> I figure that since Mages with preparation basically are physical gods anyways, and my players have played Mage since it's release originally, there is no reason to introduce enemies in my game for the purpose of fighting them, since most fights start and end like:<br /> <br /> &quot;The enemy leaps out of the shadows, blade raised in murderous inten-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;lol I had Time 2 prepared to predict an enemy, I respond with a 30 successes Forces attack at him.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He's dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> Therefore, I am much more interested in enemies that provide them with interesting contrasts and story hooks for furthering their personal plots and the like.<br /> <br /> That scene I listed up there, was for example, what started the Progenitor on the path to her first Seeking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:02:42-07:00","id":998671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=998608#post998608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get the belief that this was halfway aimed at my &quot;Nephandi are sympathetic post&quot;, so I'll respond like it was that:<br /> <br /> The game that I've been running since 1999 is not a game where objectively evil mages who are evil because they are evil will have any impact, because it's a game with basis heavily in questioning the world and questioning morality. If I use a mage who kicks puppies and murders people for the sake of being an asshole, my players will murder him and go &quot;wow, nice switch to DnD there ManusDomine&quot;, and possibly laugh at me.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Nephandi who act like human beings can get the players to question whether they are in the right, during a given situation or not. For example: I had a war veteran who had grown weary of killing (what he saw as) the same enemy in different clothes over and over, and had simply decided that humanity didn't deserve to exist any more, having seen personally how the effects of warfare looked. He was a broken man, and he had absolutely no chance at reaching his goal of anihilating humanity, even if the players didn't intervene. But he did give us this scene:<br /> <br /> Nephandus (missing a leg and lying on the ground): &quot;Why are you doing this? Can't you see they're a <i>disease</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> Suzanne Bachmayer, Damage Control Agent: &quot;Because I must, and because I cannot allow someone like you to destroy everything we have worked for.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nephandus: &quot;But can't you see what they have <i>done?</i> They take beauty and make it into weapons! They take men and make them into hollow puppets of war, who would rather kill and smile than talk to another human! They tear apart the guts of nature and use the waste for weapons! <i>Why do you condone this!?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Suzanne (now aiming her Mjolnir at his forehead): &quot;Because the vision of humanity you have seen, is the vision of a soldier, looking at the waste of humanity, while the vision I have seen, is the vision of an a doctor who knows her duty. I cannot let you live, because to do so would be to lay judgement on an entire species for the actions of a minority and beyond me. I would rather let COMMAND sit with the button that creates the apocalypse than I would that anyone else possesses it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nephandus (now crying): &quot;But can't you see!? The only purpose of humanity is to breed so that they can murder so that they can breed and murder even more! There is no greater purpose than this! Letting them live is a cruelty! A deliberate torture of the world! You are not sparing innocents that cannot defend themselves! You are condoning murderers and rapists and monsters that haven't yet tasted the sweetness of hatred! Why are you <i>DOING THIS!?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Suzanne (fires the pistol and ends him in one shot): &quot;Because if not the Union? Who then?&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously neither of these have a perfect idea of what the world is supposed to look like, and obviously the Union isn't necessarily good, but this situation outlines perfectly what I want from Mage; which is people with good intentions doing horrible things &quot;for a higher cause&quot; and &quot;a better world&quot; no matter the cost. And in this vision of the world, Nephandi are people who have played the zero-sum game and realized the Objective Truth (just like the Traditions' Objective Truths and the Union's Objective Truth...) that mankind isn't worth it, and that burning it down would be the best option.<br /> <br /> But they don't necessarily act like corruptive assholes, who rape and kill and murder. In fact, rather many of them are upstanding moral paragons.<br /> <br /> But this is by no means the canon Nephandi, since my game is heavily houseruled anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting villain, but simply isn't a Nephandi. It actually works better as a different faction entirely. Perhaps as a fanatical splinter of the Traditions. A splinter of the Verbena who think humans are a cancer in Mother Earth. A splinter faction of the Sons of Ether who view the humans species as an empirically, scientifically verifiable doomed species who need to be culled so that a superior species can evolve in their place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:22:44-07:00","id":998674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=998671#post998671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting villain, but simply isn't a Nephandi. It actually works better as a different faction entirely. Perhaps as a fanatical splinter of the Traditions. A splinter of the Verbena who think humans are a cancer in Mother Earth. A splinter faction of the Sons of Ether who view the humans species as an empirically, scientifically verifiable doomed species who need to be culled so that a superior species can evolve in their place.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I mentioned before; I don't really care for the canon Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Specifically not M20 Nephandi, or most Revised Nephandi.<br /> <br /> I like my Nephandi as people who take a look at the world and go: &quot;If the thoughts of Sleepers control the world, then this shitty worthless world, must mean that the Sleepers want oblivion.&quot;<br /> <br /> If he doesn't fit as a canon Nephandus?<br /> <br /> Good! That was never the intention.<br /> <br /> I don't want to add new Traditional factions, because of those there are plenty (and besides, he was a Technocrat), and I don't want to use the canon &quot;acceptable to murder no&quot; Nephandi, because if I wanted to play a murderhobo with license to kill, I'd go play DnD. In fact I am so completely uninterested in enemies that are acceptable targets, that I forget how canon Nephandi work most of the time, and had to go and reread M20's Nephandi chapter to even <i>write</i> that post.<br /> <br /> So, yeah he totally isn't a <i>canon </i>Nephandus. He is an actually interesting enemy that exists for other purposes than kill puppies and laugh at it.<br /> <br /> (Oh, and by the way: Since Nephandus is a masculine word, the plural is Nephandi, while the singular is Nephand<i>us</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:37:39-07:00","id":998756,"title":"","content":"Heck, that sounds like a canon Euthanatos, not a canon Nephandi. A Euthanatos could totally be working to relieve the suffering of the world by killing its excess inhabitants. I could also see a member of the Syndicate making a similar argument because of the economic drain of overpopulation and the unnecessary suffering caused by overpopulation.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting for a campaign to use a secret joint Euthanatos-Syndicate conspiracy that seeks to reduce the human population. The goal would be to reduce the human population to two billion. Objectively, they would desire an average population density of 45 people per square mile by continent (since Antarctica does not possess a permanent population). Asia and Europe have the largest population densities, followed by Africa, South America, North America, and Oceania.<br /> <br /> Since Asia has the highest population density, over 500 people per square mile, it would be the logical first targer. By reducing Asian population densities to 45 people per square mile, they would kill off over 3.6 billion people. The only question for them would be to develop a merciful method of killing that would not destroy the existing infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:49:20-07:00","id":998763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=998756#post998756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, that sounds like a canon Euthanatos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Euthanatoi kill people for their karma.<br /> <br /> What you're looking for is &quot;canon Verbena&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;The masses put a strain on Mother Earth! We must free her from this suffering!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:11:56-07:00","id":998768,"title":"","content":"Not really. Karma accumulates from suffering. People gain positive karma from suffering and gain negative karma from causing suffering. Euthanatos could see all of the suffering caused by overpopulation and come to the inevitable conclusion that the karmic cycle will break because it cannot withstand the weight of so much positive karma earned by so much suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T09:04:34-07:00","id":998788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=998768#post998768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Karma accumulates from suffering. People gain positive karma from suffering and gain negative karma from causing suffering. Euthanatos could see all of the suffering caused by overpopulation and come to the inevitable conclusion that the karmic cycle will break because it cannot withstand the weight of so much positive karma earned by so much suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A): Positive karma is called dharma.<br /> B): That is like, not at all how you accumulate karma <i>or </i>dharma.<br /> C): Karmic cycle will break? Inevitable conclusion? I am mystified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:25:05-07:00","id":998812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=998788#post998788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .<br /> C): Karmic cycle will break? Inevitable conclusion? I am mystified.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he or she means that it is &quot;inevitable&quot; in the minds of some fanatical splinter faction of the Euthanatoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:34:43-07:00","id":998835,"title":"","content":"Dharma is not positive karma, Dharma is best translated as the behaviors that lead to the accumulation of positive karma (if you are Hindu or Sikh) or cosmic laws (if you are Buddhist or Jian), though there is no central definition of Dharma, as it a complex philosophical/religious concept that changes with each religion and that has evolved with time. A central belief in Tibetian Buddhism is that suffering removes negative karma and, after a certain point, excess suffering generates positive karma (it is belief shared with many sects of Hinduism as well). As for the breaking of the karmic cycle, the goal of the Demon Lords/Yama Kings is to break the Great Cycle (which is a symbol of the karmic cycle), and they are doing so by increasing suffering in the world (at least according to canon in cWoD).<br /> <br /> Of course, any group of Euthanatos who allied with a group of Syndicates to eliminate 75% of the human population would not be mainstream Euthanatos. At best, they would be a secret cabal of a couple hundred Euthanatos would be allied with a similarly secretive cabal of a couple hundred Syndicates. Each group would be considered treasonous by their faction and would face resistance from the larger supernatural community, though they might have a chance of convincing the Fera (as less humans would be better for Gaia) and the Changeling (less humans equals less Banality) to ally with them, depending on the methodology of the conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T02:30:25-08:00","id":999134,"title":"","content":"Of course, one would hope that Euthanatos would grasp that overpopulation isn't a real problem and that Malthus was blowing smoke.<br /> <br /> One would hope that Syndicate would be able to point to real existing research that shows that population growth declines as standard of living improves, and that it is better to simply improve the global standard of living than it is to engage in genocidal slaughter.<br /> <br /> A nephandi, however, might push for the genocidal slaughter. Euthanatoi or Syndicate types who fell for Aya Tari's reasoning would then be utter <i>dupes</i> which makes a lot more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:42:21-08:00","id":999232,"title":"","content":"Malthus was not blowing smoke, it is just that he could not imagine that people would be willing to sacrifice the entire biosphere to continue to expand the population, despite what it would do to the standard of living of the average human being. 500 years ago, the average person in region that makes up the Europe Union was not that much better off than the average person in India. A sixteen fold increase in population later, the average citizen of the European Union earns 22 times as much as the average citizen of India. The problem is that most of the people in the developing world are just exist, as they are either workers who are cheaper than robots, slum dwellers, or subsistence farmers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:05:19-08:00","id":999283,"title":"","content":".... Ok, explain japan.<br /> <br /> <br /> Malthusian theory can't do that, erego Malthus is nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:13:40-08:00","id":999285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=999283#post999283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... Ok, explain japan.<br /> <br /> <br /> Malthusian theory can't do that, erego Malthus is nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, Names have power do not call him nonsense use the phrase \u201cMalthus is not perfect\u201c instead.<br /> <br /> Semper Servus<br /> Nonsense<br /> <br /> P.S.: In Essence a Nephandus can be human if his Paradigm allows it and no Quiet or Paradox Flaw says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:44:14-08:00","id":999351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=999232#post999232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malthus was not blowing smoke, it is just that he could not imagine that people would be willing to sacrifice the entire biosphere to continue to expand the population, despite what it would do to the standard of living of the average human being. 500 years ago, the average person in region that makes up the Europe Union was not that much better off than the average person in India. A sixteen fold increase in population later, the average citizen of the European Union earns 22 times as much as the average citizen of India. The problem is that most of the people in the developing world are just exist, as they are either workers who are cheaper than robots, slum dwellers, or subsistence farmers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the answer is genocide? Eugenics? <i>That's</i> going to go over well.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.forbes.com/sites/larahoffmans/2011/10/31/7-billion-reasons-malthus-was-wrong/#6771ef91560b\" target=\"_blank\">7 Billion Reasons Malthus Was Wrong</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ourfiniteworld.com/2012/12/12/why-malthus-got-his-forecast-wrong/\" target=\"_blank\">Why Malthus Got His Forecast Wrong</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/why-malthus-is-still-wrong/\" target=\"_blank\">Why Malthus is Still Wrong</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.economist.com/node/11374623\" target=\"_blank\">Malthus the False Prophet</a><br /> <br /> There are a lot of problems with how people in the developing world are being treated, employed, etc., but this doesn't make Malthus right. Despite what you said, standard of living overall has been increasing while population growth has been decreasing. This isn't uniform, of course, but it is a current trend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:56:40-08:00","id":1000020,"title":"","content":"Would a Widderslainte have a harder or an easier time pretending to be human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T03:46:52-08:00","id":1000203,"title":"","content":"A widderslainte (indeed any Nephandi) <i>is</i> human, despite what some earlier posts claim. I think the better question is &quot;Would a widderslainte have a harder or an easier time pretending to be a normal person?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T08:22:14-08:00","id":1000278,"title":"","content":"People throughout history have been able to balance being horrible people in the real world and come back to their families and treat them like decent human beings. I don't see it as impossible for a Nephandi to form the necessary thoughts and beliefs that allow them to be a <i>genuine</i> June or Ward Cleaver at home. I just think that if the PCs confronted them with the paradox in an attempt to make them feel guilt, they'd shrug and put a bullet in their family's heads, or poison the meatloaf or light their home on fire at midnight while everyone was still in bed. They just wouldn't feel guilty about that, the Caul prevents that.<br /> <br /> As to that making them inhuman? That's up to you. I think that labeling something 'inhuman' is a no true scotsman kind of thing. It makes you feel good because it distances you and the people you care about from what someone else does, ignoring the fact that there's nothing actually intrinsic to humanity that is preventing anyone from being horrible evil people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T09:26:59-08:00","id":1000296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1000278#post1000278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to that making them inhuman? That's up to you. I think that labeling something 'inhuman' is a no true scotsman kind of thing. It makes you feel good because it distances you and the people you care about from what someone else does, ignoring the fact that there's nothing actually intrinsic to humanity that is preventing anyone from being horrible evil people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that if you are easily invoking the No True Scotsman argument, you haven't made your Nephandi inhuman enough. If there is a line between human and inhuman, the Nephandi should be right there straddling that line, some because they still have a tenuous grip on humanity, and some because they cleared the line long ago and are just resurfacing for their own sick amusement.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi have multiple purposes in Mage, but one of them is to be the exception that proves the rule. In a game about moral shades of gray, they might be real evil. In a game where everyone has a valid point of view, they might not. Certainly, it is useful to offer the hope that they might be misguided or repentant, but that hope should be inextricably chained to a yawning void of hopeless, devouring malice. You can argue that even with that void they are still human (the Nephandi often do) but you can't know that. You can never know what being a Nephandi is without becoming one.<br /> <br /> Then it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:00:07-08:00","id":1000337,"title":"","content":"Well, going through the transformation of the Caul pretty much makes Nephandi inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:54:00-08:00","id":1000373,"title":"","content":"Yeah but how do you define 'inhuman'? Every attempt I've seen has been a &quot;you'll know it when you see it&quot; sort of definition, but that's notoriously inexact. I think it's a buzzword people use to label people that do horrible things so that they can say it's okay to hate them. A Nephandi who tempts people further into sin and debauchery where the ultimate goal is to turn them into jaded perverts willing to sell their souls to the infernal lords from their opium pit is just as human as one who moves through businesses encouraging 'productivity' that is basically slavery with a fresh coat of paint to management. You don't have to be a Nephandi to be his deep in human trafficking and exploitation, the Nephandi just do it for exoteric metaphysical reasons instead of mundane reasons.<br /> <br /> There's nothing stopping them from having a perfectly normal family life that they go home to, since real people that do those things often do just that. I'm sure if someone in their family found out what exactly they were doing at work, they'd be horrified but the Nephandi would either convert or kill them without a twinge of guilt.<br /> <br /> Or by 'inhuman' do you mean someone who does evil things that normal humans can't do because they don't have access to spheres? There's no practical difference between a Nephandi, a Tradition Mage or a Technocrat who uses Mind Magic to manipulate people, or who uses Entropy to cause bad destinies or Spirit to cram evil spirits into people, they're all still human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:50:35-08:00","id":1000389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1000373#post1000373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but how do you define 'inhuman'? Every attempt I've seen has been a &quot;you'll know it when you see it&quot; sort of definition, but that's notoriously inexact. I think it's a buzzword people use to label people that do horrible things so that they can say it's okay to hate them. <b>A Nephandi who tempts people further into sin and debauchery where the ultimate goal is to turn them into jaded perverts willing to sell their souls to the infernal lords from their opium pit is just as human as one who moves through businesses encouraging 'productivity' that is basically slavery with a fresh coat of paint to management. You</b> don't have to be a Nephandi to be his deep in human trafficking and exploitation, the Nephandi just do it for exoteric metaphysical reasons instead of mundane reasons.<br /> <br /> There's nothing stopping them from having a perfectly normal family life that they go home to, since real people that do those things often do just that. I'm sure if someone in their family found out what exactly they were doing at work, they'd be horrified but the Nephandi would either convert or kill them without a twinge of guilt.<br /> <br /> Or by 'inhuman' do you mean someone who does evil things that normal humans can't do because they don't have access to spheres? There's no practical difference between a Nephandi, a Tradition Mage or a Technocrat who uses Mind Magic to manipulate people, or who uses Entropy to cause bad destinies or Spirit to cram evil spirits into people, they're all still human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the term inhuman (at least how I'm applying it, and this might be an incorrect grasp on quick/fast psychology) is more a reference to extreme Psycopathy. Even the typical human can do terrible acts. Human trafficing, slavery, selling drugs, murder (even mass murder like in war), so on and so forth. But a lot of criminals don't typically do evil acts just for the sake of evil. Of course there are serial murders who kill just for the joy of killing. But your typical criminal does have a somewhat understandable reason for their actions. Money, goods, status, power, sexual desire, etc. You really don't run into a lot of people that do bad just for the sake of it. Who want to corrupt the world to see it burn.<br /> <br /> But where I see the Nephandi is being unrelatable people whose goal is the corruption and destruction of the world. And not for some reward, but because they are depraved, amoral people. A typical person doesn't enjoy murder and usually has a degree of empathy. A measure of conscious. The difference between a hitman who kills for money or a serial murder that just likes seeing people die. That human who is encouraging productivity more often than not is trying to obtain any of those previously listed human goals.<br /> <br /> The original question being asked wasn't whether or not a Nephandi could pretend to have a family. But whether or not Nephandi might still care for a family in the same way a typical human would. So in that way I think they're inhuman. A normal human can't really relate to someone like that. They can't usually even understand the mindset it would take to lack all morals. A typical human does possess a level of empathy for other people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:02:29-08:00","id":1000393,"title":"","content":"Yes, the best thing you can do with such a person is to lock them up where they cannot harm anyone else for the rest of their life. I would say, however, that Nephandi are even worse than them though because of the soul inversion caused by the Cauls. Even psychopaths have a residual human soul while Nephandi do not because their souls have been inverted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:25:46-08:00","id":1000407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1000203#post1000203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A widderslainte (indeed any Nephandi) <i>is</i> human, despite what some earlier posts claim. I think the better question is &quot;Would a widderslainte have a harder or an easier time pretending to be a normal person?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that on a spiritual level a Widderslainte is not wholly human. They seem to have little to no choice in being malicious individuals, and from birth they feel the pull of one of the Widderslainte Essences, which aren't the natural Essences of humans - but ones that exist because of the Inversion. Their Inverted Avatar is also active from the start in influencing them, which is a wholly alien state compared to normal human beings.<br /> <br /> As to them pretending to be a normal person, the Essences - Destruction, Frozen, Chaotic, Tormented - don't seem to lend well to this. Chaotic Essence description has &quot;<i>All systems are bad and need to be destroyed, all order must be subverted, and wherever there are two bricks on top of one another, they need to be knocked down.</i>&quot; etc. I can see Frozens being good at maintaining a mask of normalcy, but at the same time it's noted that they give even their fellow Widderslaintes the creeps - so highly emphatic people, or people who try to get close to them, might relatively easily notice that they are not normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:58:58-08:00","id":1000527,"title":"","content":"But a Widderslainte can still go for the long con, can't they? Even if their Avatar Essences are corrupt, Nephandi have to be able to subvert and corrupt others mages over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:06:33-08:00","id":1000707,"title":"","content":"Widderslainte are incapable of subtlety, that is for the converts. They are the upper class of the Nephandi because they were born inverted. Until they Awaken though, they may be able to fight against the nature of their inversion, especially if they have a loving environment, but I would imagine that their homes become abattoirs after they awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T07:10:43-08:00","id":1001344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1000373#post1000373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but how do you define 'inhuman'? Every attempt I've seen has been a &quot;you'll know it when you see it&quot; sort of definition, but that's notoriously inexact. I think it's a buzzword people use to label people that do horrible things so that they can say it's okay to hate them. A Nephandi who tempts people further into sin and debauchery where the ultimate goal is to turn them into jaded perverts willing to sell their souls to the infernal lords from their opium pit is just as human as one who moves through businesses encouraging 'productivity' that is basically slavery with a fresh coat of paint to management. You don't have to be a Nephandi to be his deep in human trafficking and exploitation, the Nephandi just do it for exoteric metaphysical reasons instead of mundane reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, inexact definitions happen all the time. Doesn't mean they aren't there. Just because you can't say how many grains of sand you need for a heap doesn't mean heaps aren't real. Also, it's the very metaphysical reasons you mention that make Nephandi inhuman. No matter how hard you try you can never really understand why Nephandi do the things they do. Any psychological profile of them will be wrong. Take the most depraved, psychotic, and sociopathic person you can find and there will still be an abyss between them and a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T11:33:43-08:00","id":1001408,"title":"","content":"Yet only the Avatar gets inverted, the rest is basically still a freaked out human.<br /> Following your logic would mean that everyone with an awakened Avatar can't get profiled right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:33:29-08:00","id":1001430,"title":"","content":"Speaking from a purely practical point of view, there is no real reason to make the Neph's human. If you want a human who worships demons, just use an Infernalist who hasn't reached the point of becoming an Nephandi and who has no intention of ever doing so.. If you want a complex villain with surprisingly empathetic goals, make a fanatical splinter group of one of the Traditions. The Nephs serve a very specific niche and don't need to be altered to fit other niche's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T23:01:12-08:00","id":1001637,"title":"","content":"A good point. An Infernalist can be a complex villian, there are good reasons to accept damnation as well as selfish reasons, and not everyone who deals with demons needs to be a caricature. In the American South, folktales often talk about the ease of dealing with the Devil, no special rituals or sacrifices, just a willingness to sell your soul to fulfill a driving purpose. I have often used the Man at the Crossroads in my games as an NPC who offers free advice to the characters and, on occasion, the Deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T01:00:47-08:00","id":1001665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1001344#post1001344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, inexact definitions happen all the time. Doesn't mean they aren't there. Just because you can't say how many grains of sand you need for a heap doesn't mean heaps aren't real. Also, it's the very metaphysical reasons you mention that make Nephandi inhuman. No matter how hard you try you can never really understand why Nephandi do the things they do. Any psychological profile of them will be wrong. Take the most depraved, psychotic, and sociopathic person you can find and there will still be an abyss between them and a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>IDK, I just don't find characters who are basically just extreme misanthropes drunk on a nhilistic outlook with magical powers to be<i> that difficult</i> to grock. Nephandi are as perfectly human as the next person if you take into consideration that they've been spiritually broken by other evil people and have had their Avatars convinced through magical, irreversible brainswashing that the universe and everything in it is inherently evil and the best way to fight it is to degrade it and tear it all down. An Avatar's only influence on your actions is just being a voice in your soul giving you insights into how the universe works. When you have one that takes the shape of an angel that exhorts you to righteous and holy behavior, you probably join the celestial chorus. If that same angel themed avatar is run through a caul, it still exhorts you to righteous and holy behavior, but it's opinions on what constitutes righteous' and 'holy' have undergone a drastic shift.<br /> <br /> They're people who have been put through a reverse Ludovico technique that makes their avatar convinced that everything good is a lie. It's <i>horrible</i>, but it isn't inhuman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T01:54:27-08:00","id":1001678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1001665#post1001665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IDK, I just don't find characters who are basically just extreme misanthropes drunk on a nhilistic outlook with magical powers to be<i> that difficult</i> to grock. Nephandi are as perfectly human as the next person if you take into consideration that they've been spiritually broken by other evil people and have had their Avatars convinced through magical, irreversible brainswashing that the universe and everything in it is inherently evil and the best way to fight it is to degrade it and tear it all down. An Avatar's only influence on your actions is just being a voice in your soul giving you insights into how the universe works. When you have one that takes the shape of an angel that exhorts you to righteous and holy behavior, you probably join the celestial chorus. If that same angel themed avatar is run through a caul, it still exhorts you to righteous and holy behavior, but it's opinions on what constitutes righteous' and 'holy' have undergone a drastic shift.<br /> <br /> They're people who have been put through a reverse Ludovico technique that makes their avatar convinced that everything good is a lie. It's <i>horrible</i>, but it isn't inhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to read that I'm not alone here.<br /> I think inhuman Nephandi are not needed (no problem with an occasional inhuman Nephandus).<br /> If you need something inhuman then you can use a spirit, bygone, demon etc. all of them can seem human, but are not.<br /> A Nephandus is much more worthwhile if taken as a mirror. On Marauders I think likewise.<br /> <br /> All of the above is of course in my opinion.<br /> But I think it is valid in terms of WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:48:19-08:00","id":1001696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1001637#post1001637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good point. An Infernalist can be a complex villian, there are good reasons to accept damnation as well as selfish reasons, and not everyone who deals with demons needs to be a caricature. In the American South, folktales often talk about the ease of dealing with the Devil, no special rituals or sacrifices, just a willingness to sell your soul to fulfill a driving purpose. I have often used the Man at the Crossroads in my games as an NPC who offers free advice to the characters and, on occasion, the Deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite simply, different stories need a Darth Vader, an Emperor Palpatine, or both. Different stories need a Red Skull, a Magneto, or both. Different stories need a Joker, a Ra's Al Ghul, or both. Nephs fit the niche of absolute evil, beyond ruthless fanatics with a noble end-goal, beyond even mere Infernalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:39:19-08:00","id":1001722,"title":"","content":"Yes, I agree. Now, an Infernalist can be many of those villains, but a Nephandi cannot. Even the Joker is more human than a Nephandi, as he has shown whimsical manifestations of love and mercy throughout his decades long career of crime and terror (though the Joker of the 1989 Batman movie could be considered to be a Nephandi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:53:44-08:00","id":1001728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1001722#post1001722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I agree. Now, an Infernalist can be many of those villains, but a Nephandi cannot. Even the Joker is more human than a Nephandi, as he has shown whimsical manifestations of love and mercy throughout his decades long career of crime and terror (though the Joker of the 1989 Batman movie could be considered to be a Nephandi).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 20, page 224, The Fallen:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Man is a virus pretending it\u2019s a saint. Our dreams are jokes the universe laughs about in its sleep. Beneath every good man or woman\u2019s fa\u00e7ade is an ape with a scorpion\u2019s tail. We are, in short, a mistake. And the Fallen are glad to tell us so.<br /> <br /> They probably won\u2019t tell you to your face. As a rule, <b>they\u2019re more subtle than that. Instead, a Nephandus wins your trust, gives you gifts, provides every overture of friendship. He won\u2019t come screaming out of the darkness with veins in his teeth, although he\u2019ll be glad to point you at someone who will.</b> No, the true Fallen mage is like Lassie with Joker venom \u2013 a loyal companion until the moment his poison kicks in and you both laugh yourselves to death.<br /> <br /> He doesn\u2019t expect to get out of this alive. When Creation burns, he\u2019ll burn too. But see, that\u2019s his choice \u2013 he knows the fire\u2019s coming, and he would rather be a flamethrower than kindling. The Nephandic Path is not a state of Ascension but of Descent: a willing embrace of the Void, which the Fallen sometimes call the Absolute. A Nephandus, then, has shared communion with that Absolute and has become the heat-death of the universe in human form. It doesn\u2019t matter what you do, he believes. You were worm-meat and ashes before you were born. The gods are insane and justice is a lie, and the evidence supports his point of view. He is, then, perhaps the most dangerous creature in the World of Darkness: a mage with dark truths on his side.<br /> <br /> Those who\u2019ve heard of the Nephandi imagine them as mad-eyed, screeching weirdos babbling about Outer Gods as they slash up some poor virgin\u2019s rack. It\u2019s true that some Nephandi fit that description, but those folks are primarily distractions.<b> A typical Nephandus is the enemy you won\u2019t see coming\u2026 or, if you </b><b>do, you\u2019ll want to trust him. He\u2019s probably attractive, usually well-off, and possessed of charismatic confidence. He knows</b><b> he\u2019s right with the surety of a sociopathic fundamentalist, and he doesn\u2019t give a fuck about rules or consequences. As a result, he\u2019s incredibly appealing.</b> People will give literally all they can to be with him\u2026 or to be him\u2026 and that\u2019s where his power lies. Sure, he\u2019s got magick if he needs it, but that appeal is his greatest weapon. </div> </div> </div>This completely contradicts your statement. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T07:07:52-08:00","id":1001746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1001665#post1001665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Avatar's only influence on your actions is just being a voice in your soul giving you insights into how the universe works. When you have one that takes the shape of an angel that exhorts you to righteous and holy behavior, you probably join the celestial chorus. If that same angel themed avatar is run through a caul, it still exhorts you to righteous and holy behavior, but it's opinions on what constitutes righteous' and 'holy' have undergone a drastic shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the only effect you think an Avatar has? An active Avatar can bombard a Mage with demands, criticisms and riddles. It can manipulate perceptions, manifest to the character, and drop the Mage into a mindscape (Seeking) without warning. Even a normal Avatar can obscure the lines between hallucination and reality, and the demanding ones can be a nightmare to work with. Nephandi have to deal with all of that, but in the hands of something vicious, incoherent, and broken.<br /> <br /> Being a Nephandi is a constant nightmare even without examining the &quot;Enlightenment&quot; that inverted Avatars pursue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T07:40:19-08:00","id":1001752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1001746#post1001746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the only effect you think an Avatar has? An active Avatar can bombard a Mage with demands, criticisms and riddles. It can manipulate perceptions, manifest to the character, and drop the Mage into a mindscape (Seeking) without warning. Even a normal Avatar can obscure the lines between hallucination and reality, and the demanding ones can be a nightmare to work with. Nephandi have to deal with all of that, but in the hands of something vicious, incoherent, and broken.<br /> <br /> Being a Nephandi is a constant nightmare even without examining the &quot;Enlightenment&quot; that inverted Avatars pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those things<i> compel</i> behavior though. The Barrabi were all broken by experts in corruption into willingly walking into a Caul and inverting their avatars. Widderslainte are born with poisoned conscience. Both those things make a mage unable to recognize the flaws in their avatar's advice as flawed, indeed they think that their inverted avatars are better able to understand how the universe functions than the uncorrupted magi. Nephandi wouldn't be nearly as universally evil if you took out half of the Inverted Avatar + Corrupted Morals equation.<br /> <br /> None of that makes them <i>inhuman</i> though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:28:14-08:00","id":1001767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1001752#post1001752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of those things<i> compel</i> behavior though. The Barrabi were all broken by experts in corruption into willingly walking into a Caul and inverting their avatars. Widderslainte are born with poisoned conscience. Both those things make a mage unable to recognize the flaws in their avatar's advice as flawed, indeed they think that their inverted avatars are better able to understand how the universe functions than the uncorrupted magi. Nephandi wouldn't be nearly as universally evil if you took out half of the Inverted Avatar + Corrupted Morals equation.<br /> <br /> None of that makes them <i>inhuman</i> though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly not compel. It's an open question if even the strange Avatars of Marauders compel. They do coerce, though. And manipulate. And prevent. And shift the mage's perceptions, intuitions, and instincts so that they are so far removed from human experience that they cannot be empathized with. And keep the Mage in the dark about which figure in his never ending psychosis actually is the Avatar. <br /> <br /> This isn't an issue of how evil the Nephandi are. It isn't an arbitrary number of puppies you can kick before you become inhuman. If a Nephandi and an Infernal spend their lives doing the exact same evil things, the Infernal will still be more human. The Nephandi are inhuman because they are broken and unrelatable; because no amount of empathy or understanding will help you see why they do what they do. <br /> <br /> Make no mistake, I'm not saying the Nephandi should be gibbering monsters. They can look like anything. They can fit in anywhere. They can pretend to be human, but humans cannot pretend to be them. The Nephandi would say that is because they've grown beyond humanity. The fear should be that they are right.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:28:07-08:00","id":1001855,"title":"","content":"The question is not if a Nephandi can appear human, but if a Nephandi can be human. If necessary, I am sure that the majority of Nephandi can appear to be normal people up until the time that you discover the flayed corpses stacked in their basement. Widderslainte, however, probably do not see the necessity of such deception and leave the subtle work to the barrabi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T12:52:26-08:00","id":1001887,"title":"","content":"Nephandi are human. They don't become another <i>species</i> by inverting their avatars, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:33:15-08:00","id":1002002,"title":"","content":"Well, that depends on how many modifications they decide to make. Nephandi could technically use Life to change their genetic in order to subtly incorporate nonhuman features to the point where they would effectively become another species. Since Nephandi do not seem to be that concerned with biological reproduction, they are nihilists after all, I imagine that you could get some freaky alterations. Anyway, being human is more than human biology, it is also human psychology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T23:11:46-08:00","id":1002135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002002#post1002002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that depends on how many modifications they decide to make. Nephandi could technically use Life to change their genetic in order to subtly incorporate nonhuman features to the point where they would effectively become another species. Since Nephandi do not seem to be that concerned with biological reproduction, they are nihilists after all, I imagine that you could get some freaky alterations. Anyway, being human is more than human biology, it is also human psychology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling that goalposts are being moved in this discussion. Like there was talk about how nephandi can't pretend to be normal until it was pointed out that they can and do pretend to be normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-12-2016, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T04:24:52-08:00","id":1002175,"title":"","content":"No, the goalpost was can the Nephandi 'be' human, can they have and maintain loving relationships, not 'act' human. I would say that the act of love is antithetical to the existence of the Nephandi. You can look at the write up of Nephandi Consors and Acolytes in Ascension's Right Hand to see how Nephandi treat people close to them.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are nihilists who desire to destroy everything that is human and replace it with something else. It may be the rule of the Demon Lords, the Corruption of the Wyrm, or the madness of the Outer Dark, but it is something else. The Inversion of their Avatars twists their perceptions of everything to fit their ideology of the Other. If you want a sympathetic villain, use an Infernalist, Nephandi really should only be used as the masterminds of evil for evil's sake because that is the only way they can understand the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:50:01-08:00","id":1002588,"title":"","content":"To put an absolute metapattern on something is quite limiting in my opinion.<br /> Why do you have to make all Nephandi inhuman (or evil for that matter)?<br /> Thinking in nice categories is comforting, but for the most part not really the way it is.<br /> <br /> But as always in Mage:<br /> You can't do what your paradigm disallows.<br /> This is not bad, Roleplaywise it is often very good.<br /> <br /> But the utilitarian nihilists will catch you by surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:10:04-08:00","id":1002618,"title":"","content":"I think that any alliance with the Nephandi will always seem to cost nothing, but it will end up costing more than your soul. They are more than evil, because evil people want to have a world to conquer. It is better to sell your soul to the Demon Lords than to ally with the Nephandi, at least it is only your soul that will be lost, and your sacrifice might end up doing some good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:29:57-08:00","id":1002624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002588#post1002588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put an absolute metapattern on something is quite limiting in my opinion.<br /> Why do you have to make all Nephandi inhuman (or evil for that matter)?<br /> Thinking in nice categories is comforting, but for the most part not really the way it is.<br /> <br /> But as always in Mage:<br /> You can't do what your paradigm disallows.<br /> This is not bad, Roleplaywise it is often very good.<br /> <br /> But the utilitarian nihilists will catch you by surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, its not, because nothing is stopping you from making an Infernalist villain. An Infernalist can be, and indeed usually is, very human. An Infernalist can be that guy that makes little deals with demons for the power to help his family. An Infernalist can be that guy who knows he is damning his soul, but the world needs the Technocracy/Traditions defeated RIGHT NOW or the world is doomed, so his soul is the sacrifice he's making to save the world. An Infernalist can be everything some people seem to want the Nephandi to be for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T14:23:47-08:00","id":1002639,"title":"","content":"And the ability to 'maintain loving relationships' isn't a perquisite for 'being' human. I have met plenty of miserable misanthropes who have no one because they've alienated everyone close to them. I don't think it's accurate to point to the inverted avatar and say 'this makes the Nephandi inhuman'. I don't think the Nephandi loose any horror whatsoever if you say that they're just horribly evil people with abhorrent goals and methods. The nephandic tragedy is that no one was able or willing to step in and give someone a reason not to enter the Caul, not that they're <b>EEEEEVVVVVIL</b>. Stripping them of their humanity seems to me to be an easy way out for when you kill them so that you don't have any in character guilt for killing another human being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:14:44-08:00","id":1002656,"title":"","content":"By killing Nephandi you further their goals.<br /> Imagine for a moment that Gilgul is a lie brought up by a Nephandus.<br /> I don't say that it is, but it is possible that Gilgul only severs the Avatar instead of shattering it...<br /> <br /> You are welcome to stop and think before you kill an \u201cobviously\u201c EVIL Nephandus.<br /> Even if you are right about inhuman EVIL, your murder and the resonance of it change you towards EVIL a bit.<br /> Every. Time. You. Kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:27:36-08:00","id":1002660,"title":"","content":"I do not think that mundane actions create magical Resonance, but I could be wrong. Anyway, one of the problems with killing Nephandi is finding them. If Mages are 1:100,000, what are Nephandi? On the Earth, 1:10,000,000? Which means that there might be 57 of them running around North America.<br /> <br /> Nephandi shpuld be the bogeyman because they are rarely encountered. Players should encounter evidence of Nephandi, the political conspiracies and the murderous cults, but they should rarely directly encounter Nephandi unless the players are so awful that they are targets for recruitment. <br /> <br /> Infernal Mages, however, are probably much more common that Nephandi. If Nephandi are 1% of Mages, Infernal Mages may be anywhere from 3% to 9%. Which means that they are much more likely to be directly confronted by the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:48:32-08:00","id":1002669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002656#post1002656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By killing Nephandi you further their goals.<br /> Imagine for a moment that Gilgul is a lie brought up by a Nephandus.<br /> I don't say that it is, but it is possible that Gilgul only severs the Avatar instead of shattering it...<br /> <br /> You are welcome to stop and think before you kill an \u201cobviously\u201c EVIL Nephandus.<br /> Even if you are right about inhuman EVIL, your murder and the resonance of it change you towards EVIL a bit.<br /> Every. Time. You. Kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not the way that works?<br /> <br /> To borrow from Pact, there's a difference between death and destruction.<br /> <br /> To go back to Mage, let's say there is a Celestial Chorister. Pillar of his community, gives to the poor and fights back the darkness in his community.... But he has two enemies. One the Technocratic Amalgam of his city, and two a Widderslainte who happens to be in the area.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Amalgam could break down the door, and make him disappear. He would be dead, but his memory would live on. People would still think back and go &quot;That guy was a swell dude.&quot; Or at worst, wouldn't remember him at all.<br /> <br /> The Widderslainte would not be so merciful. Not only would Joe Celestial die in an agonizing and degrading way, but everyone would look back and see his works tainted. Every thing he once stood for would be seen as a lie, as a cover for some depravity. Joe Celestial, as he existed before would be utterly gone. And all that would be left would be a twisted mockery of that, teetering on the edge of an abyss, only standing so long as to draw others closer.<br /> <br /> To go back to Pact, in Pact there is an equivalent to the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> they're called Diabolists, and they summon Demons. What's so bad about that you ask? Demons <i>destroy.</i> They do not merely kill you, they unmake what you are. And they do it in such a manner that the destruction is contagious. Things close to you inch that much closer to your fate. And so every victory for a demon takes all of reality just that one step closer to oblivion.<br /> <br /> And, as a counter-example, there are Scourges. These people summon Bogeymen, which are, long story short, every sadistic horror movie trope made living. They are terrifying, they are murderous, they are unclean.... they feed on fear, death and injury. but ultimately, they aren't causing destruction so much as they cause <i>change</i>. The change is unpleasant, but a living person dying doesn't mean what they were is gone, anymore than them trimming their fingernails does.<br /> <br /> It's a fine line. But still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T00:37:29-08:00","id":1002793,"title":"","content":"I agree <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> that death and destruction are worlds apart.<br /> But my point is that each time you cause the death of a Nephandus you do something that is \u201cevil\u201c.<br /> And thus you change yourself towards evil. Even if only a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T00:54:48-08:00","id":1002796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002793#post1002793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> that death and destruction are worlds apart.<br /> But my point is that each time you cause the death of a Nephandus you do something that is \u201cevil\u201c.<br /> And thus you change yourself towards evil. Even if only a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>The human soul isn't a container that slowly fills up from bad behavior. Nephandi, regardless of the question about their humanity, are flat out downright evil. Any negitive karma you might accrue from killing them is vastly outweighed by their death and all the people they now will be unable to corrupt and degrade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T04:10:57-08:00","id":1002825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002660#post1002660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that mundane actions create magical Resonance, but I could be wrong. Anyway, one of the problems with killing Nephandi is finding them. If Mages are 1:100,000, what are Nephandi? On the Earth, 1:10,000,000? Which means that there might be 57 of them running around North America.<br /> <br /> Nephandi shpuld be the bogeyman because they are rarely encountered. Players should encounter evidence of Nephandi, the political conspiracies and the murderous cults, but they should rarely directly encounter Nephandi unless the players are so awful that they are targets for recruitment.<br /> <br /> Infernal Mages, however, are probably much more common that Nephandi. If Nephandi are 1% of Mages, Infernal Mages may be anywhere from 3% to 9%. Which means that they are much more likely to be directly confronted by the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that nephandi should be rarely encountered seems to be the idea that PCs shouldn't be exceptional. Why shouldn't the PCs run into nephandi that often? Don't use statistics, because there are lies, damned lies, and statistics. Speaking in terms of Mage as presented, nephandi are a significant source of enemies. There's no particular reason that they should be rare <i>for PCs</i> to encounter. Especially if PCs are having all the adventures (which they should be because they're <i>PCs</i>).<br /> <br /> That is to say I think you're approaching this from a different angle than the game intends. Also, I don't think there's any source that establishes a precise census of either nephandi or infernalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T04:16:44-08:00","id":1002828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002175#post1002175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the goalpost was can the Nephandi 'be' human, can they have and maintain loving relationships, not 'act' human. I would say that the act of love is antithetical to the existence of the Nephandi. You can look at the write up of Nephandi Consors and Acolytes in Ascension's Right Hand to see how Nephandi treat people close to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if you read back in the thread you will see people claiming that nephandi can't even &quot;act&quot; human, which clearly they can and do.<br /> <br /> As well, nephandi <i>are</i> human, but are twisted. They don't stop being human because of that twisting. I think making them completely inhuman essentially destroys what horror value they do have. Only humans can be mages, after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:05:23-08:00","id":1002853,"title":"","content":"I doubt that there is any particular angle that Mage intends. The primary metaplot is Tradition versus Technocracy, but that is only one angle of the game that people can explore. As for PCs being exceptional, they are Mages. Mages are exceptional because they have the ability to defy reality, so I do not really think that they need to be more exceptional than that.<br /> <br /> I think that it cheapens the horror of the Nephandi to make them anything but inhuman. The inversion of the Avatar and the resulting corruption of the soul is an attack against everything that most people consider to be human. Nephandi, in many ways, prove that humanity is a concept that is measured in terms other than biology and genetics.<br /> <br /> I think that it also cheapens the horror of the Nephandi to make them so common that one is discovered every week by the PCs. In the Mage games that I used to run, I would use a single Nephandi as the mastermind, one that would be confronted at the end of the chronicle. The PCs would find that their normal enemies were criminals, cultists, formori, and sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:07:15-08:00","id":1002854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002639#post1002639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the ability to 'maintain loving relationships' isn't a perquisite for 'being' human. I have met plenty of miserable misanthropes who have no one because they've alienated everyone close to them. I don't think it's accurate to point to the inverted avatar and say 'this makes the Nephandi inhuman'. I don't think the Nephandi loose any horror whatsoever if you say that they're just horribly evil people with abhorrent goals and methods. The nephandic tragedy is that no one was able or willing to step in and give someone a reason not to enter the Caul, not that they're <b>EEEEEVVVVVIL</b>. Stripping them of their humanity seems to me to be an easy way out for when you kill them so that you don't have any in character guilt for killing another human being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we're just having a semantic discussion on what it means to be inhuman. I don't think anyone (besides one post last page) is implying that the description of inhuman was intended to mean they are literally not humans. Inhuman<br /> adjective 1.lacking qualities of sympathy, pity, warmth, compassion, or the like; cruel; brutal: an inhuman master.<br /> I don't disagree with you that having relatable or understandable villains can be a powerful addition to the game. But I think you're overlooking the impact that an unapologetic evil character can have. A serial murder isn't meant to be a sympathetic villain either, but I think the movie Seven shows the horror one can do rather well. While you might not feel guilty about killing them, what they do can play a different role.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:30:41-08:00","id":1002861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002853#post1002853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that there is any particular angle that Mage intends. The primary metaplot is Tradition versus Technocracy, but that is only one angle of the game that people can explore. As for PCs being exceptional, they are Mages. Mages are exceptional because they have the ability to defy reality, so I do not really think that they need to be more exceptional than that.<br /> <br /> I think that it cheapens the horror of the Nephandi to make them anything but inhuman. The inversion of the Avatar and the resulting corruption of the soul is an attack against everything that most people consider to be human. Nephandi, in many ways, prove that humanity is a concept that is measured in terms other than biology and genetics.<br /> <br /> I think that it also cheapens the horror of the Nephandi to make them so common that one is discovered every week by the PCs. In the Mage games that I used to run, I would use a single Nephandi as the mastermind, one that would be confronted at the end of the chronicle. The PCs would find that their normal enemies were criminals, cultists, formori, and sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it cheapens the horror of the nephandi to make them not-human. It turns them into pure monsters and nothing else, and robs them of their dramatic impact.<br /> <br /> Also, you completely misunderstood what I was saying about how often nephandi can and should occur. The thing is that if you want a game where nephandi are the primary enemies, you can have players face as many as you want. The idea that they should be so rare that players can only encounter them once in a chronicle is ridiculous. PCs are themselves rarer than just about everything else, and that they're typically exceptional and have exceptional adventures. So you can have games where they're rare as hen's teeth, but you can easily have games in which they're encountered more frequently and not ruin the game. There is not a <i>one true way</i> to do these things.<br /> <br /> And I know how Mage works, I ran a mage chronicle for several years, and transitioned the chronicle from second edition to revised (at least with <i>some </i>rules, not with much metaplot). The PCs fought nephandi at various points without the chronicle collapsing under their weight, nor with them being the chronicle's ultimate villains.<br /> <br /> Nephandi should be <i>whatever the ST needs them to be</i>. Not necessarily rare bogeymen, nor necessarily under every rock. They aren't one and all blood-drenched inhuman monsters and many present a fairly normal but charismatic facade. How else would they sell their perspective to prospective nephandi?<br /> <br /> Anyway, nephandi are still basically human, despite the inversion of their avatar. The thing about awakened avatars is not everyone has one, so using the state of an awakened avatar to define humanity is not a particularly convincing argument. It's like trying to argue that homid kinfolk aren't human because they're related to werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:30:18-08:00","id":1002945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002639#post1002639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the ability to 'maintain loving relationships' isn't a perquisite for 'being' human. I have met plenty of miserable misanthropes who have no one because they've alienated everyone close to them. I don't think it's accurate to point to the inverted avatar and say 'this makes the Nephandi inhuman'. I don't think the Nephandi loose any horror whatsoever if you say that they're just horribly evil people with abhorrent goals and methods. The nephandic tragedy is that no one was able or willing to step in and give someone a reason not to enter the Caul, not that they're <b>EEEEEVVVVVIL</b>. Stripping them of their humanity seems to me to be an easy way out for when you kill them so that you don't have any in character guilt for killing another human being.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi are about more than one kind of horror. Cautionary tale, enemy within the gates, friend you never knew, loss of identity, choice you can never come back from... the Nephandi are all of that and more. And much of their potential comes because you can't tell what they are. The point is not that the Nephandi <i>are</i> inhuman, the point is that you can't say for sure. You don't get the easy answer of saying they are inhuman monsters you can shoot on sight (although you should anyways), and you don't get the slightly harder answer that they are still somewhere on the range of humanity. Eliminate either one and you destroy much of their horror.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:39:01-08:00","id":1002952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997469-can-a-nephandi-still-be-human?p=1002945#post1002945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Nephandi are about more than one kind of horror. Cautionary tale, enemy within the gates, friend you never knew, loss of identity, choice you can never come back from... the Nephandi are all of that and more. And much of their potential comes because you can't tell what they are. The point is not that the Nephandi <i>are</i> inhuman, the point is that you can't say for sure. You don't get the easy answer of saying they are inhuman monsters you can shoot on sight (although you should anyways), and you don't get the slightly harder answer that they are still somewhere on the range of humanity. Eliminate either one and you destroy much of their horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complete agreement, except for the part in brackets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:31:54-08:00","id":1010133,"title":"","content":"dunno about naphandi, probably no, but infernalists probably can. As far as I remeber, the Jade Demon kept a whole harem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}